64002 #edb/ref 1069 "e-15070" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064002 #edb/ref 1071 "Factor the quadratic expression $10a^2 + 11a + 3$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064002 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "44cf8c85-f228-5eaa-922d-613355cb7d5b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064002 #edb/ref 1074 "We must factor the quadratic expression\n$10a^2 + 11a + 3$.\n\nFirst, we find two numbers that\n\n- multiply to the product of the quadratic coefficient and the constant ($10 \\times 3 = 30$), and\n- add to the linear coefficient ($11$).\n\nSince all coefficients are positive, we only need to consider the positive factor pairs of $30$.\n\nThe positive factor pairs of $30$ are\n$(1,30), \\quad (2,15), \\quad (3,10), \\quad (5,6)$.\n\nNotice the numbers in the factor pair $(5,6)$ add to $11{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n5 + 6 &= 11✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we write the linear term as $5a + 6a$, and factor the result by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n10a^{2} + 11a + 3 &=  \\\\\n10a^{2} + 5a + 6a + 3 &=  \\\\\n(10a^{2} + 5a) + (6a + 3) &=  \\\\\n5a(2a + 1) + 3(2a + 1) &=  \\\\\n&= (5a + 3)(2a + 1)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064003 #edb/ref 1069 "e-15072" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064003 #edb/ref 1071 "Factor the expression $3x^2 - 16x + 16$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064003 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "ad032833-ecf8-5295-9a9f-f69f759c19b0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064003 #edb/ref 1074 "We must factor the quadratic expression\n$3x^2 - 16x + 16$.\n\nFirst, we find two numbers that\n\n- multiply to the product of the quadratic coefficient and the constant ($3 \\times 16 = 48$), and\n- add to the linear coefficient ($-16$).\n\nSince the linear coefficient is negative and the product of the quadratic coefficient and constant is positive, we only need to consider the negative factor pairs of $48$.\n\nThe negative factor pairs of $48$ are\n$(-1,-48), \\quad (-2,-24), \\quad (-3,-16), \\quad (-4,-12), \\quad (-6,-8)$.\n\nNotice the numbers in the factor pair $(-4,-12)$ add to $-16{:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n(-4) + (-12) &= -16✓\n\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we write the linear term as $-4x - 12x$, and factor the result by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n3x^{2} - 16x + 16 &=  \\\\\n3x^{2} - 4x - 12x + 16 &=  \\\\\n(3x^{2} - 4x) - (12x - 16) &=  \\\\\nx(3x - 4) - 4(3x - 4) &=  \\\\\n&= (x - 4)(3x - 4)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064004 #edb/ref 1069 "e-15073" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064004 #edb/ref 1071 "Factor the quadratic expression $2c^2 + 15c - 8$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064004 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "35bedd9f-bcb7-5024-bfe7-5ef6d34518bc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064004 #edb/ref 1074 "We must factor the quadratic expression\n$2c^2 + 15c - 8$.\n\nFirst, we find two numbers that\n\n- multiply to the product of the quadratic coefficient and the constant ($2 \\times -8 = -16$), and\n- add to the linear coefficient ($15$).\n\nFirst, we find the factor pairs of $-16{:}$\n$(1,-16),\\quad (-1,16), \\quad (2,-8), \\quad (-2,8), \\quad (4,-4)$\n\nNotice the numbers in the factor pair $(-1,16)$ add to $15{:}$\n\n$$\n(-1) + 16 = 15 \\quad {\\color{green}\\checkmark}\n$$\n\nThen, rewrite the linear term as $-c+16c$, and factor the result by grouping:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n2c^{2} + 15c - 8 &=  \\\\\n2c^{2} - c + 16c - 8 &=  \\\\\n(2c^{2} - c) + (16c - 8) &=  \\\\\nc(2c - 1) + 8(2c - 1) &=  \\\\\n&= (2c - 1)(c + 8)\n\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064247 #edb/ref 1037 #edb/ref 17592186049074 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064247 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064476 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064247 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064577 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064247 #edb/ref 1038 #edb/ref 17592186064613 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064247 #edb/ref 1039 "Factoring Trinomial With Positive Coefficients" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186064247 #edb/ref 1041 #edb/ref 17592186064002 #edb/ref 17592186045417